---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Investors - DAJC"
  description="Investor overview of DAJC, the provider-neutral execution layer being developed for European heavy and oversized transport."
>
  <main class="investors-page">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="investors-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">DAJC · INVESTOR OVERVIEW</p>
      <h1 id="investors-heading">Building the execution layer for European heavy and oversized transport.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        DAJC is developing a provider-neutral digital environment for coordinating heavy and oversized transport
        across Europe. The goal is to connect operational participants, trusted data, documents and workflow state
        around one transport identity — without requiring carriers to replace the systems they already use.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button--primary" href="mailto:miroslav@dajc.eu?subject=DAJC%20Investor%20Materials">Request investor materials</a>
        <a class="button" href="/partners">Explore Integration Ecosystem</a>
      </div>
      <p class="availability">Detailed investor materials are available directly on request.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="overview" aria-labelledby="overview-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">The opportunity</p>
        <h2 id="overview-heading">A fragmented operational environment needs a common execution layer.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards cards--three">
        <article>
          <p class="card-label">Problem</p>
          <h3>Too many disconnected workflows</h3>
          <p>
            Heavy and oversized transport depends on permits, route constraints, vehicles and trailers, infrastructure,
            operational documents, service providers and jurisdiction-specific requirements. The information needed to
            execute a transport is often spread across separate systems, organisations and communication channels.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="card-label">DAJC approach</p>
          <h3>Coordinate — do not replace</h3>
          <p>
            DAJC is being designed as a system of engagement around existing systems of record. TMS, ERP, telematics,
            accounting, identity and other customer systems remain in place while DAJC coordinates the transport workflow
            and the information needed to execute it.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="card-label">Positioning</p>
          <h3>Provider-neutral by design</h3>
          <p>
            DAJC is not being built as a freight marketplace or broker. The architecture is intended to connect multiple
            providers and operational participants so that customers can preserve their existing technology and supplier
            relationships.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="status" aria-labelledby="status-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">Current stage</p>
        <h2 id="status-heading">Active development with public evidence of progress.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="status-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="status-number">01</span>
          <h3>Platform development</h3>
          <p>
            DAJC Platform is under active development. Customer access is not being released before 4 January 2027.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="status-number">02</span>
          <h3>Testing registration</h3>
          <p>
            Registration is open for relevant professionals and companies to participate in pre-production testing
            beginning 4 January 2027.
          </p>
          <a href="/testing">Testing 2027 &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="status-number">03</span>
          <h3>Integration ecosystem</h3>
          <p>
            DAJC publicly documents integration areas and only identifies specific providers when their public
            identification and integration status are confirmed.
          </p>
          <a href="/partners">View integrations &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="status-number">04</span>
          <h3>Public intelligence</h3>
          <p>
            DAJC.eu already publishes public operational information and project updates while the commercial Platform
            continues to be developed separately.
          </p>
          <a href="/intelligence">Explore Intelligence &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="business" aria-labelledby="business-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">Commercial direction</p>
        <h2 id="business-heading">Recurring software access, with commercial terms published only when confirmed.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p>
            DAJC is being developed as a commercial software platform for organisations involved in European heavy and
            oversized transport. The intended model is based on recurring access to the DAJC Platform, with selected
            data and integration arrangements evaluated separately where appropriate.
          </p>
          <p>
            DAJC intentionally does not present provisional pricing, unconfirmed delivery dates or detailed roadmap
            functionality as commitments. Confirmed commercial terms will be published on DAJC.eu when appropriate.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/pricing">Current public access information &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <aside>
          <p class="aside-label">Target ecosystem</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Heavy and oversized transport operators</li>
            <li>Dispatch and transport coordination teams</li>
            <li>Permit, escort and specialist service providers</li>
            <li>Vehicle, trailer and equipment ecosystems</li>
            <li>Telematics, routing, infrastructure and operational data providers</li>
            <li>Ports, ferry, customs and regulated freight-workflow participants</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="founder" aria-labelledby="founder-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Founder</p>
        <h2 id="founder-heading">Built from direct heavy-transport experience.</h2>
        <p>
          DAJC was founded by Miroslav Dajč and is being shaped from first-hand operational experience in heavy and
          oversized road transport. The product direction starts with the practical coordination problems encountered
          before and during real transports, then translates them into a provider-neutral digital workflow.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/news/platform/why-dajc-exists">Read why DAJC exists &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="materials" aria-labelledby="materials-heading">
      <p class="section-kicker">Investor materials</p>
      <h2 id="materials-heading">Continue the conversation with the detailed DAJC materials.</h2>
      <p>
        Investment memo, pitch deck and additional project information are shared directly with relevant investors
        rather than published as unrestricted public documents.
      </p>
      <div class="materials-actions">
        <a class="button button--primary" href="mailto:miroslav@dajc.eu?subject=DAJC%20Investor%20Materials">Request investor materials</a>
        <a class="button" href="mailto:miroslav@dajc.eu?subject=DAJC%20Investor%20Introduction">Contact the founder</a>
      </div>
      <p class="contact">
        Miroslav Dajč · Founder · <a href="mailto:miroslav@dajc.eu">miroslav@dajc.eu</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="notice" aria-label="Investor information notice">
      <p>
        This page is a public project overview, not an offer of securities or investment advice. Information about
        DAJC's development reflects the current public status and may change as the project evolves.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .investors-page {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    max-width: 1120px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 8vh 1.5rem 8vh;
  }

  .hero {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto 5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-kicker,
  .card-label,
  .aside-label {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.17em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dajc-orange);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    color: var(--dajc-white);
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 19ch;
    margin: 0 auto 1.4rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5.4vw, 4.2rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: var(--dajc-muted);
    font-size: clamp(16px, 2vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .hero-actions,
  .materials-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin-top: 1.8rem;
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 46px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--dajc-orange);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--dajc-orange);
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .button--primary {
    background: var(--dajc-orange);
    color: var(--dajc-dark);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .button:hover,
  .button:focus-visible,
  .text-link:hover,
  .text-link:focus-visible {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .availability {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    color: var(--dajc-muted);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .overview,
  .status,
  .business,
  .founder,
  .materials {
    margin-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .section-heading {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .section-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3.5vw, 2.55rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
  }

  .cards {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .cards--three {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .cards article,
  .status-grid > div,
  .business .split,
  .founder,
  .materials {
    border: 1px solid var(--dajc-line);
    background: rgba(0, 38, 92, 0.16);
  }

  .cards article {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .card-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .cards p:not(.card-label),
  .status-grid p,
  .business p,
  .founder p,
  .materials > p,
  .notice p {
    color: var(--dajc-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .cards p:not(.card-label),
  .status-grid p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .status-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .status-grid > div {
    min-height: 210px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .status-number {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--dajc-orange);
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .status-grid a,
  .text-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--dajc-orange);
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .business .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(280px, 0.7fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.3rem);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .business p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .business aside {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--dajc-line);
  }

  .aside-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  }

  .business ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--dajc-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .founder,
  .materials {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
    padding: clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    border-radius: 10px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .founder p {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 1rem auto 0;
  }

  .materials {
    border-color: var(--dajc-orange);
    background:
      linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(239, 125, 0, 0.1), rgba(0, 38, 92, 0.22) 55%),
      rgba(0, 20, 52, 0.45);
  }

  .materials > p {
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: 1rem auto 0;
  }

  .contact {
    margin-top: 1.3rem !important;
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .contact a {
    color: var(--dajc-white);
  }

  .notice {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--dajc-line);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .notice p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .cards--three,
    .status-grid,
    .business .split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .business aside {
      padding: 1.5rem 0 0;
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--dajc-line);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .investors-page {
      padding: 6vh 1.1rem 7vh;
    }

    .hero,
    .overview,
    .status,
    .business,
    .founder,
    .materials {
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    }

    .button {
      width: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
